1. THE RELEASED DATA AND DOCUMENTATION  —  CC BY 4.0
================================================================================

The Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0) covers
the material the VLUN authors authored inside the released set: the project's
own factual compilation, its analysis, its documentation, its schemas, its
decision records and its independently written digests. That is the released
paths under `distribution_v1/`, `docs/`, `schema/`, `V3/`, `V4/` and
`_audit/`, the repository's own documents, and every other released path the
manifest marks `project_own`, `metadata_only` or `attribution_required` other
than the authors' own code covered by part 2.

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You are free to share and adapt this material, including commercially,
provided you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate
whether changes were made.

SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0

**This grant does not cover, and licenses, nothing of the following, wherever
it occurs — including inside a path the manifest marks as released:**

  * copied third-party source text (Solidity, Rust, Move, Cairo, Vyper and
    the rest), quoted or otherwise;
  * proof-of-concept code written by third parties;
  * fixing diffs copied from third-party repositories;
  * third-party report prose: audit findings, titles, impact statements,
    remediation advice and mined PDF passages;
  * personal data of named individuals.

Where the released set carries a short third-party quotation, the manifest
marks that path `attribution_required`: reuse must attribute the original
author. See part 4 for why attribution is not a redistribution right.

